    {
      "title": "India's core sector growth hit 31-month high of 10.9% in October",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/core-sectors-growth-rises-to-10-9-in-oct-coal-iron-ore-key-drivers-126112000852_1.html",
      "description": "Output of key infrastructure industries rose 10.9 per cent in October 2026, up from 0.8 per cent in the year-ago month, driven by strong performance in coal, iron ore, electricity and cement.\nAccording to the official data released by the Commerce and Industry Ministry on Friday, the core sector expanded by 8.2 per cent in September 2026.\nAmong segments, iron ore output rose by 26.4 per cent, electricity by 21.6 per cent, coal by 23.1 per cent, and cement by 15.4 per cent.\nDuring April-October this fiscal, these nine segments expanded by 6 per cent against 2.3 per cent in the same period last year.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T11:57:59"
    }
